From a53208d81466f854fa5c91545ab02e62517b50d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark <30506876+markhuguet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:16:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] inkling: fused MoE routing op, residual add folded into the
 short-conv fusion, fewer decode launches

- GGML_OP_MOE_ROUTE (ggml_moe_route_ids / ggml_moe_route_weights): top-k(sigmoid + bias) expert ids and the
  normalized sigmoid weights of the selected + shared experts (CPU + CUDA/HIP; ids and weights in one launch when
  adjacent). Replaces ~14 routing ops per MoE layer. LLAMA_INKLING_NO_MOE_ROUTE=1 builds the old op chain.
- rel-position bias via out_prod: no per-token transposed copy of attn_rel_proj (bit-identical).
- CUDA/HIP sconv fusion also folds the following residual ADD (GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_SCONV_RESIDUAL_FUSION=1 to turn
  off), and refuses to fuse when the output overlaps the state/kernel/cache it reads across channels.
- shared-expert down-proj views are created before the adds so the add chain fuses.
- test-backend-ops: MOE_ROUTE cases (per op and whole graph).

Decode dispatches/token 2192 -> 1438; tg64 +7.7% @0, +6.4% @4K (Q5_K trunk); decode output bit-identical except
the routing math (KLD vs f32 CPU ref 0.164 vs 0.168).
